<edge source="3D_DYNAMIC_GAF_e65a0505" target="3D_DYNAMIC_GAF_e65a0505" id="memorize_finding(finding=Consolidated summary at step 23 (for th...)">
  <data key="d3">memorize_finding(finding=Consolidated summary at step 23 (for th...)</data>
  <data key="d4">1</data>
  <data key="d5">[-0.05, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0]</data>
  <data key="d6">[[-0.05, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0]]</data>
  <data key="d7">{"finding": "Consolidated summary at step 23 (for the last block of research):\n**Strategic Lesson:**\n\n**Keep:**\n\n- The **positive correlations** with mean heldout accuracy, particularly those with high correlation coefficients (e.g., mean learning speed, mean train accuracy, number of convolutional layers, number of layers). These factors have shown a strong relationship with model performance and should be maintained and further explored.\n- The **best trial's architecture** as a baseline, given its high mean heldout accuracy (0.854) and held out test accuracy (0.796). However, consider the changes mentioned in the \"Change\" section to address overfitting and other potential issues.\n\n**Change:**\n\n1. **Address overfitting:**\n   - Implement more regularization techniques, such as higher dropout rates, L1/L2 regularization, or early stopping based on validation performance.\n   - Simplify the model architecture by reducing the number of layers or filters.\n   - Use data augmentation to increase the diversity of the training set.\n\n2. **Improve dataset and evaluation:**\n   - Ensure the dataset is balanced, or use techniques like stratified sampling, resampling, or class weights to address class imbalance.\n   - Implement cross-validation to improve the reliability of the reported accuracies.\n   - Include other relevant metrics (e.g., precision, recall, F1-score, AUC-ROC) to evaluate model performance comprehensively.\n\n3. **Enhance architecture and training:**\n   - Choose an architecture suitable for the given task, considering the data type and inductive biases.\n   - Experiment with different normalization techniques (e.g., layer normalization, instance normalization) and activation functions.\n   - Explore various optimizers (e.g., SGD, Adam, RMSprop) and their hyperparameters to improve model convergence and performance.\n\n4. **Ensure reproducibility:**\n   - Set a random seed for reproducibility and document all experimental details, including data splits, hyperparameters, and hardware configurations.\n\n**New Hypothesis:**\n\nBy addressing overfitting, improving dataset and evaluation practices, enhancing the architecture and training process, and ensuring reproducibility, we hypothesize that the model's generalizability and performance will improve. Specifically, we expect to achieve a higher heldout test accuracy with a smaller gap between train and test accuracy, indicating better generalization.\n\n**Actionable Tasks for the Next Optimization Phase:**\n\n1. Implement regularization techniques and data augmentation to address overfitting.\n2. Balance the dataset or use appropriate techniques to handle class imbalance.\n3. Conduct cross-validation and report multiple evaluation metrics.\n4. Experiment with different architectures, normalization techniques, activation functions, and optimizers.\n5. Document all experimental details and set a random seed for reproducibility.\n6. Evaluate the model's performance on a heldout test set and compare it with the previous best trial.", "experiment_name": "3D_DYNAMIC_GAF", "_data_source": "data_paper_mine_csv", "_manifest_name": "data_paper_mine_csv", "_dataset_params": {"n_fft": 256, "hop_length": 64, "gaf_image_size": 64, "video_num_segments": 8, "video_gaf_image_size": 64, "representation_type": "1D_CNN"}}</data>
  <data key="d8">[-0.05450000000000001, 0.026320822797947115, 0.004055894032982265, 1.6071263574314116, 1.9585133738594056]</data>
</edge>
